P=lambda x:'[page:%s]'%x
# --- no-go / structural
N('flow-blindness-sl2','obstruction','Flow-blindness no-go (Lemma SL2)','Phi_eps(u)=exp(-eps u^2)Phi(u) stays even, positive, log-concave, doubly-exponentially decaying, yet H_{-eps} has a non-real zero for every eps>0 (Rodgers-Tao). No hypothesis stable under small backward heat flow proves RH. Lean-checked with Lambda>=0 as hypothesis. Matches the HEAT control.','proved','no','yes',P('FlowBlindnessNoGoPage')+' src/data/flow-blindness-no-go.js',['heat-flow','lambda','antibridge','lean','de-branges'])
N('t3-zero-free-strip-dictionary','identity','T3(a) = zero-free strip dictionary (SL0/SL1)','E_a(z)=A_a(z)-iB_a(z)=Xi(z+ia). De Branges kernel of E_a is PSD iff E_a is Hermite-Biehler iff zeta has no zero with Re s>1/2+a. T3(a) for all a>0 is RH. Trig core verified to 1e-30; canonical cosh(2au) convention gives shift a (factor-2 relabel elsewhere).','proved','no','yes',P('FlowBlindnessNoGoPage')+' src/data/flow-blindness-no-go.js',['de-branges','twin-ladder','zero-free','bridge'])
N('ns-rigid-dichotomy','obstruction','Theorem NS-RIGID (native-span softness dichotomy)','P_S(eps)_ij=(phi_eps(s_i)+phi_eps(s_j))/(s_i+s_j-1), phi_0=xi\'/xi, finite S in (1,inf). Either P_S(0)>0, then P_S(eps)>0 for small eps (flow-stable, useless), or P_S(0) not PD and RH is false. Only the full family over all finite S is flow-critical, and it equals RH.','proved','no','yes',P('Imp95549NsRigidPencilEigenvalueViz')+' src/data/imp-95530-native-span-arithmetic-input-rigidity.js',['pick','heat-flow','antibridge','weil','explicit-formula'])
N('ns-rigid-primes-enter-as-n-scalars','mechanism','Primes enter native-span forms through n scalars (PICK-WEIL A1)','Every Hermitian form built from the explicit formula on the span E_V(S) is a function of P_S(0) and the Cauchy Gram; the primes enter only through the n numbers zeta\'/zeta(s_i), s_i>1. Multiplicativity is not visible to any finite node set.','proved','no','yes','src/data/imp-95530-native-span-arithmetic-input-rigidity.js (A1) '+P('Imp95549NsRigidPencilEigenvalueViz'),['pick','explicit-formula','euler-product','antibridge'])
N('ns-rigid-pencil-psd-past-lehmer','measured-phenomenon','Flowed Pick pencil stays PSD ten orders past Lehmer collision','lam_min(P_S(eps)) for nu={1,2,4}: 3.2421e-5 at eps=0, 2.900e-5 at eps=1, 3.02e-8 at eps=100; positive on eps in [1e-12,1e2], while Xi_eps has non-real zeros unconditionally for eps>1.15e-11.','measured','no','unknown',P('Imp95549NsRigidPencilEigenvalueViz'),['pick','heat-flow','antibridge'])
N('ns-rigid-lacunary-blaschke-clause','obstruction','Lacunary node sets do not reach RH (NS-RIGID A6)','If sum 1/s_k<inf (e.g. geometric lattices nu_0 rho^k), the nodes form a Blaschke sequence and Pick positivity on them only gives some Caratheodory interpolant, not F=phi. Reaching RH needs sum 1/s_k=inf (Muntz-complete sets), where the trace-class structure is unavailable. Obstruction map row P18.','proved','no','yes','src/data/imp-95530-native-span-arithmetic-input-rigidity.js (A6)',['pick','antibridge','de-branges'])
N('ns-rigid-loophole-dirichlet-coefficients','open-lemma','Loophole outside NS-RIGID: Dirichlet-coefficient inputs on the line','Inputs that consume Dirichlet coefficients on the critical line (Levinson-Conrey mollifiers, Selberg proportion, near-line density) are flow-critical, non-circular, not RH-equivalent, and not covered by NS-RIGID. Whether any such input yields an every-window statement is open.','conjectural','yes','no','src/data/imp-95530-native-span-arithmetic-input-rigidity.js (loophole)',['mollifier','euler-product','bridge','large-sieve'])
N('res-t-resolution-law','identity','RES-T fixed-support Weil-positivity resolution law','For Weil form W_T with test support T and an off-line quadruple at displacement delta, detectable height ceiling H_ceil(T,delta)=2 pi exp(E), E=delta^2 S(T delta)^4 T^3, S(x)=sinh(x/2)/(x/2). Fixed-T positivity follows from verified height only for T<T_X (about 3.88); doubly exponential in T.','proved','no','no',P('Imp95567DoublyExponentialHeightCeilingViz')+' src/data/imp-95533-res-t-standalone-lemma.js',['weil','explicit-formula','antibridge'])
N('obstruction-seam','obstruction','Obstruction seam: provable and sufficient halves do not overlap','16 angles on C_H and Montgomery PCC each split into a provable-but-inert half (on-basin, mesoscopic, |alpha|<=1, upper bound, t=0, finite height) and a sufficient-but-RH-hard half (min-gap lower bound, |alpha|>1 pair correlation, all-t displacement). No overlap found.','closed','unknown','no',P('ObstructionSeamPage')+' src/data/rh-obstruction-seam-2026-07-16.js',['pair-correlation','lambda','antibridge'])
N('lemma-w-wide-support','open-lemma','Lemma W (wide-support diagonal pair correlation)','Exist A>1, C, T0: sum_{0<gamma<=T} T^{2A|beta-1/2|} <= C T log T for T>=T0. Equivalent to zero density N(sigma,T)<=C T^{1-2A(sigma-1/2)} log^{O(1)} T with slope 2A>2. Implies a fixed strip |beta-1/2|<=delta*=(1+kappa)/(2A), kappa about 0.20, then Lambda<=2 delta*^2.','conjectural','unknown','yes',P('SubHalfStripPccCriterionPage')+' src/data/subhalf-strip-pcc-criterion-2026-07-31.js',['pair-correlation','zero-free','lambda','bridge'])
N('frozen-rung-pt-inertia','obstruction','Frozen rungs = Platt-Trudgian; inertia cannot beat verified height','ind_-(K_{R_a}) = number of xi-zeros with Re lambda>a (Krein-Langer). Schur-complement freezing preserves negative index (Sylvester), so a frozen-rung certificate on a finite mesh never exceeds verified height. Full equivalence with PT is conjectural (lemmas L1 tail leakage, L2 mesh resolution). Map rows Q6, S7.','proved','no','no',P('FrozenRungPTEquivalencePage')+' src/data/frozen-rung-pt-equivalence-2026-07-31.js',['twin-ladder','pick','lambda','antibridge'])
N('pt-floor-binds-verified-height','measured-phenomenon','Verified height binds the Lambda<=0.2 floor','Interval-rigorous audit: verified zero height X about 3e12 binds; barrier slack (margin>=1.2) and AFE tail (margin about 1.047, X-independent) do not. Lambda<=t0+y0^2/2 improves inversely with log X and cannot reach 0.','certified','no','no',P('PtFloorSensitivityAuditPage')+' '+P('VerifiedHeightLeverPage'),['lambda','heat-flow'])
N('zero-density-lambda-inert','obstruction','Zero density is Lambda-inert','A density bound is an upper bound on the number of off-line zeros and never certifies zero count 0 below height X; even the full Density Hypothesis moves the rigorous barrier bound on Lambda by zero.','closed','no','no',P('ZeroDensityScopingPage')+' '+P('GuthMaynardScopingPage'),['zero-free','lambda','large-sieve','antibridge'])
N('mollified-barrier-zero-gain','obstruction','Mollified barrier certificate: min-modulus gain exactly 0','min|Mf|/max|M| <= min|f|. A mollifier turns the phase-blind triangle bound from -0.155 to +0.206 at x0=2.83e13 but cannot beat the unmollified barrier. Longer mollifiers at fixed height have ceiling Lambda_ceil(X)=min(1, gamma ||A/B||); obstructed for y>=0.14 on the 0.145 line.','certified','no','no',P('MollifiedBarrierCertificatePage')+' '+P('Imp95770BarrierMollifierLengthCeilingViz'),['mollifier','lambda','antibridge'])
N('route7-cost-exponential','measured-phenomenon','Route VII complete-row cost is exponential in 1/t','For a complete row U=t+y^2/2, ln N1*(t,y) grows like (2c0-y)/t; the SC3 gate alone forces ln N1*>(1+sqrt(1-2t))/t. Calibrated on two Arb points to 1.6%. Reachable floor U about 0.150 (stretch 0.145).','measured','no','no',P('VizCostFloorPage')+' src/data/imp-95218-route7-cost-curve.js',['lambda','heat-flow'])
N('qrh-conditional-lambda','identity','Conditional Lambda <= 0.116091488672439 from Re s>7/8','Given zeta(s)!=0 for Re s>7/8 (Lean proof rebuilt locally, standard axioms only), an unrefereed analytic chain G0, PT verification to 3.0001753e12 and the route-P ledger: Lambda<=116091488672439/10^15. Earlier chain values 0.118505710922701 and 0.117708313410954.','certified','yes','yes',P('LambdaQrhConditionalPage')+' src/data/qrh-path-push-2026-10-08.js',['zero-free','lambda','lean','bridge'])
N('lambda-rh-ledger','identity','de Bruijn-Newman ledger','H_t(z)=int_0^inf e^{tu^2}Phi(u)cos(zu)du has only real zeros iff t>=Lambda; RH iff Lambda<=0; Lambda>-inf (Newman); Lambda>=0 (Rodgers-Tao); so RH iff Lambda=0. A zero-free strip of half-width delta gives Lambda<=2 delta^2 (de Bruijn Thm 13).','proved','no','yes',P('CShockNumericalCoincidencePage')+' src/data/lambda-rh-height-mapping.js',['lambda','heat-flow','zero-free'])
# --- twin ladder / bridge
N('shift-bridge-threshold','identity','Shift-bridge threshold theorem (Section 15)','X(w)=xi(1/2+w), Delta=sup|Re lambda| over zeros of X. For fixed a>0: |X(w-a)|<|X(w+a)| for all Re w>0 iff a>=Delta. RH iff the strict inequality holds for every a>0. Common zeros of X(w-a), X(w+a) give a removable zero row, permitted by semidefiniteness.','proved','no','yes',P('ShiftBridgePositivityPage')+' src/data/shift-bridge-positivity-section.js',['twin-ladder','bridge','de-branges','zero-free'])
N('four-closure-routes','identity','Four equivalent closure routes for Delta=0 (Section 16)','Equivalent for all a>0: (A) |xi(s-a)|<|xi(s+a)| for Re s>1/2; (B) shifted bridge kernel K_a PSD on C_+; (C)/(D) Schur/bounded-real and no-ghost forms. Each is RH-equivalent; they share one bottleneck.','proved','no','yes',P('ClosureRoutesPage')+' src/data/closure-routes-section.js',['twin-ladder','bridge','de-branges','pick'])
N('blaschke-ghost-negative-square','identity','Inverse Blaschke ghosts: one negative square per off-line zero','R_a(w)=X(w-a)/X(w+a), |R_a(it)|=1. Each uncancelled right-half-plane pole alpha contributes K_S(z,w)=-k_alpha(z) conj(k_alpha(w)), k_alpha(z)=sqrt(2 Re alpha)/(z-alpha). Negative index = number of ghosts, given a coprime generalized-Schur factorization (not automatic). Map row Q6.','proved','no','yes',P('BlaschkeGhostsPage')+' src/data/blaschke-ghosts-section.js',['twin-ladder','pick','bridge','de-branges'])
N('freeze-preserves-negative-index','obstruction','Schur-complement freezing preserves negative index (Prop 23.2)','Freezing as Schur-complement (Feshbach) reduction of the bridge Gram keeps the inertia: ghosts move, they do not vanish. Endpoint bridges repair only finite-window positivity (Lemma 23.3).','proved','no','no',P('FreezingBridgePage')+' src/data/freezing-bridge-section.js',['twin-ladder','pick','antibridge'])
N('hidden-square-volterra-collapse','identity','Hidden-square chain: no-ghost = Volterra contraction','A_a(z)=int Phi cosh(au)cos(zu)du, B_a(z)=int Phi sinh(au)sin(zu)du; shear density Phi(u)Phi(v)sinh(a(v-u)) on u<=v. Block [[I,V],[V*,I]]>=0 iff ||V_{a,Phi}||<=1. Seven-step forward and five-step reverse chains reduce the Section 15-27 conjectures to this norm bound.','proved','no','yes',P('HiddenSquareProgramPage')+' '+P('CollapseChainPage')+' '+P('VolterraBoundPage'),['twin-ladder','shear','bridge','de-branges'])
N('volterra-norm-threshold-closed','obstruction','Volterra norm bound: true only up to a*','Campaign result (map row P20): ||V_{a,Phi}||<=1 holds exactly for a<=a* in (31.6213,31.6214) and is false above. Earlier in-repo record: HS bound sqrt(I_0 J_a) exceeds 1 near a=2.3 (J_a ~ e^{4a}); HS within 2.02% of op norm; kernel Phi(x)Phi(y)sinh(a(x-y)) is near rank one.','closed','no','no',P('VolterraNormCurvePage')+' '+P('VolterraKernelHeatmapPage')+' '+P('SchattenTraceNormPage'),['shear','twin-ladder','antibridge'])
N('shear-gram-hollow-antisymmetric','object','Shear Gram is the hollow antisymmetric de Branges Wronskian','G_shear(u,v)=Phi(u)Phi(v)sinh(a(v-u)) is antisymmetric, zero on the diagonal, indefinite with spectrum symmetric about 0; min eigenvalue about -||G_shear|| about -4.8e-6 at NPHI=10, a=0.5, U=6.','measured','no','unknown',P('Imp3252ScaledMuPage'),['shear','twin-ladder','de-branges'])
N('hankel-gap-aU-invariant','identity','Off-diagonal endpoint-Hankel obstruction depends on s=aU only','De-homogenized R_jk=H_jk/sqrt(D_jj D_kk): substituting tau=Ux cancels U, so R, its spectrum, ||R|| and the gap ||R||-max R_jj depend on s=aU alone. Raw-monomial gap grows about 0.9 per degree (1.79 at DEG=2 to 10.8 at DEG=12): a basis-conditioning artifact.','proved','no','unknown',P('ClosureRoutesPage')+' src/data/imp-3085-hankel-gap-aU-grid.js '+P('Section26ConditioningArtifactPage'),['shear','twin-ladder'])
N('excess-fraction-onset-pole','measured-phenomenon','Excess fraction phi(s)=G(s)/F(s): quadratic onset pole','On s>s0=arcsinh(1): phi ~ C/(s-s0)^2 with C=sqrt(2)(1-arcsinh 1) about 0.16776 and tail phi ~ K e^{-s}. Integral diverges at s0; regular mass int_{s0+1}^inf phi=0.26900597 (agreement with C_shock=sqrt(2/(3 log gamma_N)) at N=1e4 is a coincidence).','measured','no','unknown',P('ExcessFractionPhiPage')+' '+P('CShockNumericalCoincidencePage'),['shear','twin-ladder'])
N('kyp-bounded-real-prime-delay','mechanism','KYP / bounded-real lift of the bridge (Apps M-O)','Bridge ratio Theta_a as transfer function of a parallel prime-delay system. Passive lift iff KYP LMI feasible (P>0). L2-dissipative iff a Lyapunov-Krasovskii functional V>=0 with dV/dt<=-||y||^2 exists, iff ||Theta_a||_inf<=1. Signed-Mobius barrier blocks the delay lift.','conjectural','yes','yes',P('KypBoundedRealPage')+' src/data/kyp-bounded-real-section.js',['bridge','twin-ladder','pick','euler-product'])
N('cayley-schur-trajectory','object','Cayley-Schur transform of the canonical-system m-function','Theta_a(z)=E_a^#(z)/E_a(z), E_a(z)=X(a-iz); Cayley(m)=(m-i)/(m+i) maps the Weyl m-function to the unit-disk Schur class (Krein, de Branges). Trajectory leaves the disk iff a zero has displacement >a.','proved','no','yes',P('CayleySchurTrajectoryPage'),['de-branges','pick','twin-ladder','visualization'])
N('reciprocal-pf-excluded','obstruction','Reciprocal total positivity: direct PF-infinity route excluded','PF_inf kernel iff 1/g(s)=e^{as^2+bs} prod(1+delta_k s)e^{-delta_k s}, delta_k>0. A certified negative 5x5 Toeplitz minor rules out PF_inf for the actual kernel; the rotated reciprocal 1/X(is) is RH-equivalent, not a reduction. Map row G4.','certified','no','yes',P('ReciprocalProgramPage')+' src/data/reciprocal-program-section.js',['lee-yang','antibridge','twin-ladder'])
N('nyman-beurling-dx','identity','Nyman-Beurling distance and reciprocal Mobius ladders','d_X^2=inf_c ||1_(0,1](x)-sum_{n<=X} c_n rho(1/(nx))||^2 in L^2(0,inf); RH iff d_X->0. M_X(s)=sum_{n<=X} mu(n)n^{-s}. Finite reciprocal constructions are compact diagnostics with no global tail or uniform margin. Map row P14.','proved','yes','yes',P('ReciprocalProgramPage'),['mollifier','euler-product'])
# --- Open frontier T-series
N('t3-residual-inequality','open-lemma','T3: exact Twin Ladder residual inequality','K_a=K_{a,0}+D_{a,R}+K_a^(S) with K_{a,0}>=0 the positive core. Prove D_{a,R}+K_a^(S)>=-K_{a,0} as Hermitian forms for every a>0 and every finite test set in C_+. D_{a,R} cancels to second order through cos(ps)-1; absolute values spend the whole core. RH-equivalent.','conjectural','unknown','yes',P('OpenFrontierPage'),['twin-ladder','shear','bridge','theta'])
N('no-psd-partition-of-core','obstruction','No PSD partition of the positive core repairs both channels','At a=1/4, z=(-1/2,0,1/2)+i/5: beta_R>1.027286016, beta_S>0.42200180358, sum>1.449>1. Radial and shear are symmetric and skew parts of one theta tensor; each integration slice is indefinite, so positivity must be theta-specific and appear only after integration.','certified','no','no',P('OpenFrontierPage'),['twin-ladder','shear','theta','antibridge'])
N('wiener-hopf-phase-condition','identity','Fixed-thickness frontier is one Wiener-Hopf phase condition','Fixed a: A_a>=0 iff X(w-a)/X(w+a) is Schur on Re w>0 iff m(lambda)<=m(lambda-2a) for every zero with Re lambda>a. A_{a_n}>=0 for infinitely many a_n->0+ iff RH. a>=1/2 holds unconditionally; B(w)=xi(w)/xi(w+1) is inner. R_{2a}(w)=R_a(w-a)R_a(w+a).','proved','no','yes',P('OpenFrontierPage'),['twin-ladder','pick','bridge','de-branges'])
N('poisson-measure-criterion','identity','RH as a Poisson representation with half-width 1/2','RH iff q(t)=int dmu(u)/((t-u)^2+1/4) for one positive weighted measure mu (from the a=1/2 inner anchor B(w)=xi(w)/xi(w+1)).','proved','no','yes',P('OpenFrontierPage'),['pick','de-branges','twin-ladder'])
N('eventual-psd-is-global','identity','Tail PSD is already global PSD','K_a restricted to [L,inf) PSD for some L iff A_a>=0 globally (real analyticity propagates). For each n there is L_{a,n} with all n-point minors positive beyond it, but the threshold depends on n and far-separated cross minors are negative.','proved','no','yes',P('OpenFrontierPage'),['twin-ladder','pick','antibridge'])
N('one-point-all-jets','identity','One point suffices iff every jet order is controlled','Fixed a: J_a^(d)(z*)>=0 for all d>=0 iff K_a>=0 globally; for a_n->0 the family over all n,d is RH. A de Branges toy kernel has positive jets to any prescribed finite order yet is globally negative: no universal finite cutoff. Compare map rows P3, S9.','proved','no','yes',P('OpenFrontierPage'),['pick','de-branges','antibridge'])
N('conformal-schur-window','identity','Verified height gives a conformal Schur window','With Y=H-1/2=3000175332799.5, c=pi/(2Y): |X(w-a)/X(w+a)|<1 on Re w>0, |Im w|<Y; the Pick kernel with sinh(cw) denominators is PSD on the strip. The original linear-denominator kernel is not established (negative real 2x2 minor).','certified','no','no',P('OpenFrontierPage'),['pick','twin-ladder','bridge'])
N('high-poles-escape-detector-bands','obstruction','High residual poles escape every fixed detector band','U_a*QU_a-Q=P_{I conj(J) K_J}-P_{K_I}: residual poles are the positive model-space component, but their compression into any fixed band tends to zero as height escapes. Fixed-band detection is not height-uniform.','proved','no','no',P('OpenFrontierPage'),['pick','de-branges','antibridge','zero-channel'])
N('staged-strip-triangular-inequality','open-lemma','Staged strip [1/8,7/8] as one triangular prime inequality','sum_{p<=x}(x-p)log p <= (x^2-1)/2 + C x^{15/8} is equivalent to the closed zero strip [1/8,7/8]; the Riesz factor makes the zero sum absolute (no log loss). Equivalent heat-trace form: sum_{m,p}(log p)e^{-pi m^2 p u} <= zeta(2)/(pi u)+C u^{-7/8}.','conjectural','yes','yes',P('OpenFrontierPage'),['zero-free','theta','explicit-formula','euler-product','bridge'])
N('prime-tent-rh-equivalence','identity','RH iff one nonnegative prime tent on (N,4N]','RH iff 2 sum_{N<p<=2N}(p-N)log p + sum_{2N<p<=4N}(4N-p)log p <= 3N^2 eventually. The dilation F(4N)-3F(2N)+2F(N) cancels primes p<=N. On RH the prime-square bias dominates the zero wave: L_+V_theta <= -(0.155951-o(1))N^{3/2}.','proved','yes','yes',P('OpenFrontierPage'),['explicit-formula','euler-product','bridge','zero-channel'])
N('zero-complete-rational-tents','identity','Zero-complete rational tents shrink the support ratio','For Q_a(s)=(a^s-1)(a^s-a) all multiplier zeros lie on Re s=0 or 1 and the prime kernel is nonnegative; RH margin positive from a=1.882453339. a=17/9: RH iff 17 sum_{81N<p<=153N}(p-81N)log p+9 sum_{153N<p<=289N}(289N-p)log p<=127296N^2 eventually. Certified supports 529/225, 1024/441; floor b*=3.4513363850.','certified','yes','yes',P('OpenFrontierPage'),['explicit-formula','euler-product','bridge'])
N('two-tents-joint-zero-completeness','mechanism','Two positive tents remove each other\'s blind multiplier zeros','c=124/123, m=61,62: multiplier polynomials have exact gcd (z-1)(z-c). Their eventual prime signs together are RH-equivalent although one generic positive tent may hide an off-critical mode. Concave positive annular kernels are weighted averages of single-tent ratios.','certified','yes','yes',P('OpenFrontierPage'),['explicit-formula','euler-product','bridge'])
N('pascal-carry-ballot','open-lemma','Annular cofactor as adjacent Pascal/carry mean comparison','RH iff C_N<=S_N eventually, with log(S_N/C_N)=2760N(mean_{345N<=u<529N} log K_u - mean_{225N<=u<345N} log K_u), K_u=(u+1)^u/(u! rad(u!)). K_u rises at composites, falls at primes. v_3(S_{3^L}/C_{3^L})=-4923*3^L+15, so divisibility, pairwise and per-block proofs fail; cross-factor cancellation is open.','conjectural','yes','yes',P('OpenFrontierPage'),['euler-product','explicit-formula','bridge'])
N('prime-square-pole-recurrence','identity','Prime-square pole forces super-sqrt(N) runs of valid scales','Unconditionally: liminf D_{23,15}(N)/N^{3/2}<=-11081.705, liminf D_{32,21}(N)/N^{3/2}<=-40805.171 (negative residue at s=3/2 plus Landau). Each late checkpoint stays negative over floor(sqrt(N) exp(0.8 sqrt(log N))) consecutive scales; starts may be sparse, so no eventual sign.','proved','yes','no',P('OpenFrontierPage'),['explicit-formula','euler-product','zero-channel'])
N('first-radix-layer-criterion','identity','First radix layer carries the full criterion','RH iff sum_{p<=N}[C_p(N)-(N-p)]log p>=0 eventually. Radical Mellin kernel K(s)=((s-1)zeta(s)-1)/(s(s+1)), K(1)=0, K(rho)=-1/(rho(rho+1)); higher-radix tail H_N>=0, H_N ~ -zeta(1/2)N^{3/2}/3.','proved','yes','yes',P('OpenFrontierPage'),['explicit-formula','euler-product','zero-channel'])
N('mobius-deaveraging-price','identity','Mobius deaveraging has an exact fixed-power price','M(x)=O(x^{7/8} log^K x) implies R_{1,1/4}(x)=O(x^{1/8} log^K x), which would prove the staged strip; it is stronger at boundary multiplicities and not known. Multiplier zeta(2s) cannot cancel an excluded right-half zero; sparse support is prime times square.','proved','yes','yes',P('OpenFrontierPage'),['zero-free','theta','explicit-formula'])
N('jacobi-smoothing-unstable','obstruction','Jacobi smoothing is pole-faithful but exponentially unstable','Symbol |h^(tau)| ~ (1+|tau|)^{13/8} e^{-pi|tau|/2} never vanishes, so no zeta pole is cancelled, but there is no tempered inverse. A smooth positive PNT density satisfies the averaged bound with unbounded pointwise triangular error.','proved','no','no',P('OpenFrontierPage'),['theta','heat-flow','antibridge'])
N('large-sieve-density-selector','mechanism','Multiplicative large sieve closes the high-zero gap for fixed finite profiles (T153)','Each dyadic zero packet contributes O(log T/sqrt T) after normalization; natural density handles fixed low zeros. Every natural-density selector samples the same critical wave. The estimate is not uniform in zero height: the Abel difference costs |rho|.','proved','yes','no',P('OpenFrontierPage'),['large-sieve','explicit-formula','zero-channel'])
# --- Theta trap / CM flow
N('theta-trap-theorems','identity','Theta-trap theorems A/B/C for the attractive CM flow','Flow dx_k/ds=-2 sum_{j!=k}1/(x_k-x_j). Trap holds at Theta<=1/4 unconditionally (A) and at Theta<=Theta_b=(sqrt73-5)/8=0.443000 under minimal gap (B, sharp: boundary Q(Theta)=r(2r^2+7r-3), r=2Theta-1/2); isolation g<=0.72 d_1 traps every level<=1 (C). Configurations in (0.443,0.5073) cross upward.','proved','no','unknown',P('TheoremBThresholdPage')+' '+P('SpectralAttackPage')+' src/data/sg1c-theta-trap-theorems.js',['heat-flow','pair-correlation','lambda'])
N('isolation-ratio-rate-identity','identity','Exact isolation-ratio rate (Lemma R2-T) and c_glob','d(g/d_1)/ds=((g-d_1)/d_1^2)[2/(g+d_1)+4(g+d_1)/(d_1 g)] for a single nearest neighbour. Half-lattice rate bound has unique root c_glob=0.8980208880762339 of 4+4r-4/r-4/(r+1)-2[psi(1+2/r)-psi(1+1/r)].','proved','no','unknown',P('ThetaBasinClosurePage')+' '+P('OnsetBracketLedgerPage'),['heat-flow','pair-correlation'])
N('static-route-obstruction-r1t2','obstruction','Static tie comparison cannot cap the excursion (R1-T2)','On the near-uniform lattice Theta_K=K/(K+1)->1 the seizing margin tends to 0, so no static bound caps the excursion peak below 1. Open part is dynamical: whether the CM flow from zero-like data can reach a near-uniform lattice (minimality transfer). Map row P31.','proved','no','unknown',P('ThetaStaticObstructionPage')+' '+P('ThetaSeizingMarginPage'),['heat-flow','pair-correlation','antibridge'])
